1
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:17,767
North latitude, 28 degrees 24 minutes,

2
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:21,187
west longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

3
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,691
Wait for the next new moon.

4
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:29,654
This location is Cape Canaveral.

5
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:31,489
Kennedy Space Center.

6
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,410
It will be during the new moon.

7
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,579
Six more days.

8
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:40,790
My father would never let
the priest get away.

9
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,209
I am Jolyne Cujoh!

10
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:46,379
I have to seal what he took.

11
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:49,674
We are breaking out.
We're about to leave this place.

12
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,385
Take me with you then.

13
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:01,478
Good-bye, lovely Aquarium.

14
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,814
I thought it was a shithole
when I first got there.

15
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,025
But now that we're out…

16
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:09,569
- It was…
- It was…

17
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,571
- the shittiest place ever.
- the shittiest place ever.

18
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:13,990
That's a gas station.

19
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:16,117
And that's a bus stop!

20
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:18,244
Are we riding a bus?

21
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:21,206
I've never been on a bus before.

22
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,541
We're escaped convicts.

23
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:26,086
We're bound to get caught
if we hop on a bus.

24
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:30,840
But we can't exactly track down
the priest on foot.

25
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:33,426
First, we need to secure
a means of transportation.

26
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:16,029
EPISODE 25: BOHEMIAN ECSTATIC (1)

27
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:17,488
What did you say?

28
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:19,490
Weather Forecast.

29
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:21,367
Jolyne is no longer

30
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:25,163
in the prison's Female Ward
nor the solitary cells.

31
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:28,750
I can tell by the shift in the air.

32
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:31,711
It must mean that she managed to escape.

33
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,007
Hold on a second.

34
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:42,764
A star-shaped birthmark.

35
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,810
What exactly are you?

36
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:51,064
I saw the same birthmark

37
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:54,192
on the back of The Green Baby's neck.

38
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:58,404
And I've heard that Jolyne's father
also has the same mark.

39
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,866
If you can't recall, then surmise.

40
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,369
How did you end up at Green Dolphin?

41
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:07,956
You say you don't have any memories,

42
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:11,876
but doesn't that mean
the priest took your memory disc?

43
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:16,005
One thing is for certain. He's our enemy.

44
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:21,427
I will break out, track the man,
and defeat him to learn the truth.

45
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:23,763
What will you do?

46
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:31,062
Two convicts have escaped
The Green Dolphin Street State Prison.

47
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:35,441
The convicts' names are
Jolyne Cujoh and Ermes Costello.

48
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:39,862
We have released their photos
and are seeking information.

49
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:44,826
Jolyne got past Mew Mew's Stand,

50
00:04:44,909 --> 00:04:46,995
and is now coming after me.

51
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:55,169
The hell? Why won't my car start?

52
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:59,841
Got plenty of gas in the tank.
This has never happened before.

53
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,926
I've never missed a maintenance check.

54
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:15,315
Sorry, Father.

55
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:18,276
We're nowhere near your destination,
but it's as far as we can go.

56
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,361
I'll radio for another cab.

57
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:24,949
No, here is fine. I'm not in a hurry.

58
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:32,206
I've felt ill since I took on my new form.

59
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:35,126
Five days remain
until the next new moon rises.

60
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:37,712
I must keep them away,

61
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:41,132
whether it's Jolyne or someone else.

62
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:51,142
Hurry, he's in cardiac arrest!

63
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:54,103
He's a robber.
The police shot him in the leg.

64
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,105
He then jumped off
the sixth floor of the building!

65
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,864
This one's a biker gang member,

66
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:07,617
speeding on the wrong side of the road
and lost control!

67
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,368
What the hell is with tonight?

68
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:11,370
This one's a drug addict. He's in shock!

69
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:39,315
Stay back, bastards!

70
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:42,235
The drug addict woke up!

71
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:44,445
Shit, he's stabbing his hostage!

72
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:47,198
Put your gun down!

73
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:50,827
There's no way in hell
I'm getting thrown in prison!

74
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,753
Code 258.

75
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:02,922
Requesting backup at the state hospital.

76
00:07:03,005 --> 00:07:04,507
Hey fucker!

77
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:09,720
You're going to mumble
but pretend like you don't hear me?

78
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:15,226
I'm fucking pissed!
I'm shoving these scissors in his neck!

79
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:19,188
I saw shooting stars in the sky earlier.

80
00:07:20,022 --> 00:07:22,191
- There were three.
- What?

81
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:25,695
I'm quite certain.
There were three shooting stars.

82
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,115
Where did you come from?

83
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:32,952
You don't know what you are, do you?

84
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:40,209
He stabbed the hostage!

85
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:41,919
That wasn't…

86
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:46,132
No, it wasn't you,
but these scissors are positioned

87
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:49,343
a mere millimeter away
from severing my nerves.

88
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,012
This is a coincidence.

89
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:54,724
It just so happened to stab me
in a way that isn't fatal.

90
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:57,518
What will you do? It's all in your hands.

91
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,896
Will you move the scissors
ever so slightly?

92
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:04,150
Before you decide,
do you believe in gravity?

93
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:07,778
There's a gravitational force
that draws one person to another.

94
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:10,656
I have become a believer
in this very moment.

95
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,326
You cannot kill me.

96
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:16,662
You are here because
you were drawn in by my pull.

97
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:21,042
Stop wasting time on drugs.

98
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:24,545
Redirect your energy to
the things that it's intended for.

99
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:26,756
Fuck this!

100
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:38,309
You all must not know

101
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:40,811
who your father is.

102
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:43,022
Soon, you will find out.

103
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:54,534
A gravitational pull

104
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,536
draws one person to another.

105
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,601
Ouch.

106
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:25,439
My, thank you.

107
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:28,025
It's nothing serious.

108
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:33,906
It's just an old knee injury
that aches when it rains.

109
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:37,702
Your knee aches when it rains.

110
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,704
Yes, that's right.

111
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:41,706
Thank you, son.

112
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:46,002
Don't get into people's business.

113
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:49,255
Our backs may no longer have
The Green Dolphin logo,

114
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:53,217
but our jailbreak is all over the news.

115
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:57,680
We must find a car and
gain distance immediately.

116
00:09:57,763 --> 00:09:59,432
No stolen cars.

117
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:03,102
The authorities will be able to
track a stolen vehicle.

118
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,688
It will only interfere with
finding the priest.

119
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:08,482
So what, you want to take the bus?

120
00:10:08,566 --> 00:10:11,110
Are we going to wait at the bus stop?

121
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:12,903
Hey, you two.

122
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:16,324
Are you taking the bus?

123
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:18,409
The next bus is an hour away.

124
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:21,162
How about you hop onto my truck?

125
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,247
If you don't mind
sitting in the bed, that is.

126
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:26,208
You were very kind to me,

127
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,252
so I feel very good right now.

128
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:31,339
Even the pain in my knee is gone.

129
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,299
I've never felt better.

130
00:10:33,382 --> 00:10:35,176
The clouds are starting to part too.

131
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,853
Weather Forecast.

132
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:53,611
We're in luck.
Let's ride with him, Anastasia.

133
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,503
Jolyne had better be safe.

134
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:12,880
How is she getting to places?

135
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:15,549
Jolyne is headed north.

136
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:17,510
I sense that for sure.

137
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:21,347
North. We must head north.

138
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,853
There's a famous theme park
in a city up north.

139
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,146
Have you ever been?

140
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,607
That's right, you can't remember.

141
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:35,444
There's one character
who's especially famous at the park.

142
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,696
Maybe even you'd recognize him…

143
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,996
What a joke.

144
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:48,874
None of the characters are printed!

145
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:01,053
Watch out! We're not alone.

146
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,472
Could it be an enemy?

147
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,349
Diver Drive!

148
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:07,560
Got it!

149
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:13,399
Anastasia, there's more than one.

150
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,818
Either way, I caught one of them.

151
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:20,281
What the hell is it?

152
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:36,088
Search, Weather Forecast.
The Stand User must be nearby.

153
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:39,800
I doubt it's this old man.

154
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:42,052
He has no reason to stage a happenstance

155
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:44,221
just to close in on us.

156
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,849
Then someone else must be close by.

157
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:51,687
Just as you felt Jolyne's movements,
the priest must sense yours.

158
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,315
He could be sending enemies after us.

159
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:56,400
What are you? Spill it!

160
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,277
You don't want to do that.

161
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,654
It's in your best interest to not hurt me.

162
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:02,740
Children around the world will weep!

163
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:05,659
The hell was that?

164
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:07,870
Can't breathe…

165
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:11,665
Can you not choke me like that? I mean it.

166
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:16,378
There's one more of you here.
Do you work in pairs?

167
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:19,006
N-No, it's just me.

168
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:26,263
Oh, no! Sorry, my bad!

169
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,599
I didn't mean to hurt you.

170
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:29,975
Little punk!

171
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:33,395
My nose grows on its own.

172
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:35,439
It's a reflex thing!

173
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:38,984
When I lie, my nose grows.

174
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,779
Sorry, I lied just now.

175
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:44,573
I mean, it wasn't totally a lie.

176
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:49,912
Well, I don't work in a pair,
but I'm not exactly alone either.

177
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:50,829
That's right.

178
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:55,751
Oh, see that? I was telling the truth.

179
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:57,378
My nose shrank back!

180
00:13:57,461 --> 00:14:00,339
- Ouch.
- What the hell are you?

181
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:03,342
Please don't be so rough.

182
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:07,513
I'm speaking for myself here,
but I'm a good guy.

183
00:14:07,596 --> 00:14:09,932
I'm a friend to all little children.

184
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:13,185
When you were a boy,
I was your friend too.

185
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:19,108
Speaking of friends,
the seven are hiding close by.

186
00:14:19,191 --> 00:14:22,778
I saw three of the seven earlier.
See that?

187
00:14:22,861 --> 00:14:24,780
A half-eaten apple.

188
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:33,080
Weather, what the hell are they?

189
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:40,421
This apple's not poisoned.

190
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:41,839
It's safe to eat.

191
00:14:41,922 --> 00:14:44,341
You know who bit into a poison apple?
Snow White.

192
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:47,428
The bite she took is just
lodged in her throat.

193
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,305
She didn't digest the thing.

194
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:54,101
Who eats an apple
from a random old lady, anyway?

195
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:57,646
We're even wary about
Valentine's day chocolates.

196
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:01,817
She's so naive!
It makes us want to protect her.

197
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:09,033
How many are there on this truck?
There's so many of them, Weather!

198
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:12,620
Calm down. There's no need to panic.

199
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:16,248
What did you like as a child?
Did you have a favorite character?

200
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,125
I bet it was me.

201
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:21,128
I'm a fan of the T-1000 series
from The Terminator,

202
00:15:21,211 --> 00:15:22,671
not that it's with us.

203
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:24,757
We love Chewbacca.

204
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,425
Not to mention The Elephant Man!

205
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:31,138
But Snow White is the best of all!

206
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:32,640
- Heigh-ho!
- Heigh-ho!

207
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:37,603
People like to speculate
whether we're involved,

208
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:41,273
but we and Snow White have
a purely platonic friendship!

209
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,650
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

210
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:49,365
These vermin…

211
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:51,158
That means they're…

212
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:54,620
I know them. I know who they are.

213
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,914
But what could this all mean?

214
00:15:57,498 --> 00:15:58,999
Breaking news.

215
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:01,210
Today at 1:30 p.m.,

216
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:06,048
Batman has disappeared
everywhere in the world.

217
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:09,259
An investigation is underway,
with experts looking into the possibility

218
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:11,845
of ink and print fading
caused by chemical breakdown.

219
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:15,140
Similar incidents have been reported
for various characters.

220
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:19,812
Hey Weather! Is that what it is?

221
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:23,774
They came straight out of stories?
But why?

222
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:36,453
Who's your favorite? Is it me?

223
00:16:36,954 --> 00:16:39,206
Sorry, but I don't know any of you.

224
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:41,959
Now scram, unless you want me
to kick you to death.

225
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:46,171
Weather, I had that book first.

226
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:48,298
Put that apple down.

227
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,341
The book too!

228
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:52,845
Where are you, Anastasia?

229
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,639
Anastasia?

230
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:56,807
Where did you go?

231
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:00,060
Old man, stop the car!

232
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,855
- What?
- What's wrong, Weather?

233
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:04,398
I said, hit the brakes!

234
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:05,858
Oh good heavens.

235
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:08,819
- How sickening!
- This is terrible! Everyone, come look!

236
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:12,448
Old man, stop! Stop the car!

237
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,616
What? What is it, Weather?

238
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:22,958
Weather! What's happening?

239
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,878
That man under the truck!

240
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:30,632
That face! How did I fall?
How did I get there?

241
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:33,594
You split.

242
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:36,722
You were my fan, weren't you?

243
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:39,058
Way back when you were little.

244
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,476
Shit!

245
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,437
I'll get run over by the tires!

246
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:46,106
Weather, get him to stop the car!

247
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:56,283
This can't be happening.

248
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:02,831
Shit, we won't make it!

249
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:24,228
Weather Forecast made airbags.

250
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:29,566
Are you hurt?
How did you fall out like that?

251
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:33,403
It must have been a Stand attack,

252
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:36,240
but I wonder why it only targeted you.

253
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:41,203
Maybe it's got
something to do with the fact

254
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,205
that I don't recognize Pinocchio.

255
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:45,290
Hey Weather!

256
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:47,626
Am I invisible to you?

257
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:49,920
Is that me on the ground?

258
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:51,255
Are you all safe?

259
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:52,297
- Woo-hoo!
- Woo-hoo!

260
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,715
Where's the princess?

261
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:54,800
Is she okay?

262
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:58,137
She got thrown towards the burger shop.
Let's go get her!

263
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:01,056
Look up! Do you recognize them?

264
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,268
I know of them! But we aren't friends.

265
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:08,272
They're Japanese!
So sleek! Such show-offs!

266
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:11,441
Fictional characters are brought
into the real world.

267
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,193
Not only that,

268
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:16,697
they have the ability to
split our minds from our bodies.

269
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:19,116
That's what this is all about, isn't it!

270
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:23,203
If you're a Stand,
tell me where your User is!

271
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:25,747
I don't know.

272
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,500
I really don't know a thing.

273
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,127
I'm just Pinocchio.

274
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:34,840
But who cares?

275
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:38,010
You can be a hero in a fantasy.

276
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:39,720
Isn't it wonderful?

277
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:43,390
Your mind split off because
it wants to be a part of our world.

278
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:45,601
A world where everyone longs to be,

279
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:47,311
Bohemian Ecstatic.

280
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:49,688
It's a capriccio of the free!

281
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:57,738
Cut the nonsense, or else,
this is what you'll get.

282
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:03,452
What are you doing?
How could you do this to me?

283
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:06,705
All children around the world
are my friends!

284
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:10,167
This is not how the story goes!

285
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:17,424
Weather is gone.

286
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:22,262
I need to stay with him
and my body right now.

287
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:24,556
Please wait.

288
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,850
Don't go.

289
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:32,272
Sorry, old man. That crash was on you.
I'm taking off.

290
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:36,735
Hold on, I can't hear you.

291
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:41,573
I have quite a hairy ear.

292
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:44,034
Come closer.

293
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:47,329
You need to sit tight.

294
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:49,957
Onlookers will gather any minute
and will call an ambulance.

295
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:53,585
Did you hurt your finger?
Your nail is split.

296
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:56,922
No, these hands are

297
00:20:57,005 --> 00:21:00,050
for giving you a big, warm hug
as a thank you for saving me.

298
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:03,971
Your pants are ripped.
Something's sticking out of it.

299
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:06,098
It's a duster.

300
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:11,561
Let me repay you by dusting you off.

301
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:14,898
Is everything okay?
Your mouth is split to your ears.

302
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:19,403
Yes, it's to swallow you whole,
Little Red Riding Hood!

303
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,326
Diver Drive!

304
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:33,500
And that's how the story goes.

305
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:37,462
Did he just say "story"?

306
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,010
Weather!

307
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:49,850
Pinocchio and the dwarves
didn't seem to be Stands.

308
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:52,269
The User and the Stand
are in separate places,

309
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:54,855
bringing the characters to life.

310
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:59,443
To the north. I feel the presence.

311
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:02,529
The User and its Stand are not far away.

312
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:05,198
Pinocchio is only the start.

313
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,367
We must get rid of the User.

314
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:09,494
Weather!

315
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:12,205
Can't you hear me?

316
00:23:41,419 --> 00:23:46,424
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
